### Summary of Work

#### 1. Form Vocabulary in `ui` ([`ui@0.2.0`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/mesh.json#L20-L34))
- **Component Contributions**:
  - Registered [`ui.Form`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L16) (`<form novalidate>` handling submit/reset without reloads).
  - Registered [`ui.Field`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L17) (structural field container managing labels, control slots, hints, and error alerts with ARIA role `alert`).
  - Registered [`ui.Label`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L18) (native label with required indicators).
  - Registered [`ui.Select`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L19) (native select dropdown with `spaceIsTextInput: false`, immediately dispatching `input` events).
  - Registered [`ui.ButtonRow`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L20) and [`ui.Dialog`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L21) (`<dialog>` with `spaceIsTextInput: false`).
- **Reactive Props Discipline**:
  - Strictly follows `Props = Reactive<Json> | undefined` per prop.
  - Entire `style` objects are getters (`style: () => ({ ... })`).
- **Input-Driven Dispatching**:
  - Dispatches `input` events immediately on change without requiring blur.
  - Empty numeric inputs normalize to `undefined` rather than defaulting to `0`.
- **First-Class Override Seam**:
  - Implemented [`renderForm`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/views/schemaForm.ts#L26-L265) driven by JSON Schema.
  - Allows callers to refine individual fields (`label`, `hint`, `order`, `hidden`, `widget`, `placeholder`, `renderControl(ctx)` for swapping just the control widget, or `renderField(ctx)` for wrapping the field while calling `ctx.defaultField()`) or form-level elements (`fieldOrder`, `renderActions(defaultActions)`, `frame(defaultForm)`), rather than having to replace or hand-code whole forms.
- **Theming**:
  - Form styles defined in [`src/ui/ui.css`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/ui.css#L104-L248) under `@layer ui.components`.
- **Browser Tests**:
  - Verified in [`test/ui.browser.test.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/test/ui.browser.test.ts#L650-L837) (registration, reactivity, input events, empty numbers, and override seam).

#### 2. Site Editor Application ([`sites@0.1.0`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/mesh.json#L183-L215))
- **Application Architecture**:
  - Built console application in [`src/sites/`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/sites/) following the [`src/fleet/`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/fleet/) design.
  - Opens its own window on startup via `queueMicrotask` if `cx.windows.own().length === 0`.
  - Layout features an entity list on the left ([`ui.EntityList`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L10) / [`ui.EntityItem`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L11)) beside a detail surface on the right ([`ui.DetailSurface`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/src/ui/contract.ts#L12)).
- **Data Flow & Fields**:
  - Reads sites via `cx.models('site')`.
  - Configurable metadata fields: `theme`, `policy`, `title`, `description`, `indexable`, and `mesh` exposure list.
- **Release Separation**:
  - `releaseHash` is explicitly excluded from site metadata editing because binding a release to a hostname is `cdn.deploy`'s responsibility.
  - Active release deployment is handled in an independent section backed by `cdn.deploy`.
- **Server Write Blocker**:
  - Opened issue [FLYBYME/mesh-serve#5](https://github.com/FLYBYME/mesh-serve/issues/5) requesting `site.create` and `site.update` exposure (excluding `releaseHash`).
  - Form metadata editing controls and save button are visibly disabled with an informative banner explaining server pending exposure, rather than broken.
- **Confirmation Safety**:
  - Destructive mutations (deploying a release to live traffic, resetting dirty forms, or navigating with unsaved edits) prompt the user via `cx.confirmation.ask`.
- **Zero Casts**:
  - Implemented cleanly with TypeScript type guards and narrowing; zero `as any`, `as never`, or type assertions.
- **Browser Tests**:
  - Comprehensive browser tests in [`test/sites.browser.test.ts`](file:///home/ubuntu/code/mesh-core-dispatch-9/test/sites.browser.test.ts).
  - All 44 tests across all 6 test suites in the repository pass cleanly.

